# Implementation Plan - UI Refinement (Phase 2)

## Goal
Elevate the **Overlay** (text panel) and **Timeline** (playback controls) to match the new minimal Sidebar and Header. The goal is a cohesive, "studio-grade" dark editorial aesthetic.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I am proposing to move away from the "flat white" play button in the timeline to a more sophisticated glassmorphism design that aligns with the rest of the UI. I also plan to simplify the scrubber by removing the step dots for a cleaner, unified line.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] [Overlay.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/components/Overlay.tsx)
- **Softer Borders**: Reduce border opacity for a more integrated feel.
- **Improved Spacing**: Increase padding and line-height for better readability of mathematical explanations.
- **Equation Section**: Refine the separation between the description and equations for a cleaner "card" look.
- **Animations**: Tighten the crossfade duration for a snappier feel.

### [Component] [Timeline.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/components/Timeline.tsx)
- **Redesigned Play Button**: Replace the stark white background with a high-transparency glass button + glow effect.
- **Simplified Scrubber**: Remove individual step markers (the "dots") in favor of a clean, unified progress line with a subtle playhead indicator.
- **Improved Alignment**: Ensure all transport controls and the scrubber are perfectly vertically centered.
- **Cleanup**: Remove unused `RotateCcw` import.

### [Style] [index.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/index.css)
- **Update `.overlay-panel`**: Adjust the slide-in animation for a more subtle entrance.
- **Update `.timeline-bar`**: Refine the rise-in animation and hover states.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification
- No automated tests available for UI polish, will rely on visual inspection.

### Manual Verification
- Verify the Overlay feels "lighter" and equations are easier to read.
- Verify the Timeline controls feel more premium and less "boxy".
- Check responsiveness on narrower viewports.
